# Keep the build context small.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs only configs/ and build-fips-kernel.sh, so nothing here
# is at risk of being baked into the image — but the whole directory is still
# sent to the daemon on every build, and output/ holds a ~16 MB kernel image
# plus its modules tarball. Excluding it keeps `make build` and
# `make image-scan` from shipping the previous build's artifacts each time.

# VCS and CI config
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Build artifacts from a previous run
output/
*.log

# Editor, agent and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker files themselves
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# BuildKit credential staging file (dependency-resolution.md §6). The canonical
# Gitea module-credential pattern mounts these variables via
# --mount=type=secret and the file is meant to live OUTSIDE the build context;
# this line is the second line of defence, so that a copy landing in the tree
# by accident can never be baked into a layer by a broad COPY.
gomodauth*
